  "details": "Tbh i really dislike the new default avatar system that has been added. the new robots just look ugly and giving them a garish color isnt helping...\nThats why i would like to propose a new solution.\ninstead of the grey robot and slightly altered ones. Make a new selection of them, including the old robot, a vaguely male looking human, a vaguely female looking human, a robot, some kind of antho furry character, and maybe a few more based on feedback.\ncreators would be allowed to choose which one would be shown by default when their avatar isnt available on a platform. On top of this, players would also be able to override this selection with whatever model they would like a person to be with a simple choice in the quick menu. \nYou can integrate the colors into the new feature aswell, allowing creators to pick what the color of the model would be tinted to, and maybe even allowing the override of this aswell.\nTo me this would appeal to the most people, allowing those who really do want variety in the horde of grey robots, and allowing those who prefer things a certain way to choose what is shown, and allowing creators who cant or wont upload content to other platforms an easy remedy for the mismatch between a robot and whatever they uploaded.\nHopefully this concept could be taken into some consideration. Upon seeing the new garish robots i presented this idea to a few friends and they seemed to agree this would appeal to everyone.\n\nedit: oh yeah and while were at it.. can we finally get some darn legs on the robots now..? its kind of ridiculous this isnt yet a thing..",
